WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.687
Step 1. Open the Medicine Administration sub-tab.

1.2
00:00:03.687 --> 00:00:07.755
The drug chart shows the completed doses of each medicine,

1.3
00:00:07.755 --> 00:00:10.921
day by day and time slot by time slot.

2.1
00:00:10.921 --> 00:00:14.963
Step 2. Open the drug chart. Select View Drug Chart.

2.2
00:00:14.963 --> 00:00:19.812
Care opens the Drug Chart page of the patient.

3.1
00:00:19.812 --> 00:00:22.665
Step 3. Choose what the chart shows.

3.2
00:00:22.665 --> 00:00:28.088
Show discontinued medications adds the medicines that have no active entry.

3.3
00:00:28.088 --> 00:00:32.782
Time slots per day splits each day into one to four slots.

4.1
00:00:32.782 --> 00:00:34.793
Step 4. Read the chart.

4.2
00:00:34.793 --> 00:00:39.694
Care lists Regular Medications, and PRN Medications (As needed).

4.3
00:00:39.694 --> 00:00:45.324
Each cell shows one tick for each completed dose in that time slot.

5.1
00:00:45.324 --> 00:00:48.586
Step 5. Print the chart. Select Print.

5.2
00:00:48.586 --> 00:00:54.476
On a phone or a tablet that can share a PDF, the button reads Share.
